# Revision 3 (owner, 2026-10-07, docs/phase-nav-brief.md): global
# buttons, agent A (input.c/ui_main.c). NEEDS that work: on `nav` alone,
# UI_KEY_MENU only pops one level on release (never a hold-to-root), and
# a long-held UI_KEY_PLAY does nothing at all (ui_main.c's
# "!in.long_press" guard on its release-time handling skips both the
# short pause-toggle and -- there being no long-press handling yet --
# anything else), so all three cases below currently show no effect.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-nav-globalkeys.script
# needs: library

wait 4000           # boot to the main menu, "Music" selected
wait_db 30000

# -- NEXT/PREV from every screen: the track changes, the screen doesn't -
wheel +4             # "Shuffle Songs"
wait 400
key SELECT           # starts playback. NAV-H1's stub enter() calls
wait 1500            # today's gui_wps_show() path, the stock Rockbox
                     # WPS, which blocks until it is left: "key MENU"
                     # below does that (ipodui-p2-wps.script), landing
                     # back on the main menu with "Shuffle Songs" still
                     # selected
key MENU
wait 700
wheel -4             # back to "Music"
wait 400
key SELECT           # Music
wait 800
wheel +1             # "Artists"
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
shot artists_before  # browsing, audio playing in the background
key RIGHT             # NEXT: a tap skips to the next shuffled track
wait 500
shot artists_after   # the screen must be pixel-identical to artists_before
                     # (the track changed in the background; this script
                     # can't yet assert that by itself -- see the report:
                     # it needs either a playback-side sim hook, such as
                     # the current track path, or Now Playing visible for
                     # a visual check)

# -- hold MENU from three levels deep: pop to root, slide back ----------
# still in Artists (RIGHT/NEXT didn't move the screen): three pushes deep
# from the main menu once in (Music menu, Artists, an artist's albums)
wheel +5 300          # "The Bellwethers" (slow clicks, one row each)
wait 1500
key SELECT            # push: the artist's albums ("All Songs" first)
wait 800
shot three_deep
hold MENU 1000          # hold MENU: jump straight to the main menu
wait 700
shot after_hold_menu    # must be the main menu, not one level up

# -- hold PLAY: sleep (shutdown through the normal path) -----------------
hold PLAY 1000
wait 3000               # clean_shutdown()/shutdown_hw() run on other
                        # threads; give them time
shot after_hold_play

quit
